WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.764
Here is how TimeSiam works.

00:00:01.844 --> 00:00:08.592
From a single time series it randomly samples two
windows: a past subseries and a current subseries,

00:00:08.672 --> 00:00:10.913
together called Siamese subseries.

00:00:10.993 --> 00:00:16.581
The current window is lightly corrupted with a
simple augmentation such as masking.

00:00:16.661 --> 00:00:21.497
Two shared-weight Siamese encoders process the past
and current windows,

00:00:21.577 --> 00:00:29.144
and a decoder with cross-attention reconstructs the
masked current series using the past observation as context.

00:00:29.224 --> 00:00:33.787
That single design choice, reconstructing the
current from the past,

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:38.635
forces the model to internalize how distant moments
in a series relate.

00:00:38.715 --> 00:00:44.234
To handle the fact that past and current windows
can be near or far apart in time,

00:00:44.314 --> 00:00:49.492
TimeSiam adds learnable lineage embeddings indexed
by that relative distance,

00:00:49.572 --> 00:00:53.043
so one model fluently represents many temporal gaps.

00:00:53.123 --> 00:01:00.690
The training objective is simply the squared
reconstruction error between the true and predicted current series.
